{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"2026-11-01 mechanism confirmed for the f3db rejection (read-only; no host change, no Gerrit change created).\n\nMechanism: the client's view of Gerrit main was stale, so git negated an older commit and re-sent main commits Gerrit already had, with deltas against a tree from a commit that JGit's connectivity check never marks as known.\n1. 05c23655 (change 3203 ps1, parent d1a11e74) was committed 10:34:06Z. Gerrit main was 23fdf77f (merged 10:18:31Z), but this repo only fetched 23fdf77f at 10:35:32Z (refs/remotes/gerrit/main reflog). The client cannot negate an advertised tip it lacks.\n2. Gerrit advertised `.have` lines for the shared account's open changes; change 3202 (ps1 745304ad / ps2 a41975c8) had parent e5a7e75b and was present locally. So the client's boundary was e5a7e75b: it sent 05c2 + d1a11e74 + 8e2201dc, using e5a7e75b's trees as thin-pack bases. f3db49d9 is e5a7e75b:src/rebar.\n3. JGit FullConnectivityChecker.checkObjects:196 accepts an external base only if the walk flagged it UNINTERESTING: trees of advertised haves, plus trees of boundary commits. The server boundary was d1a11e74 (05c2's parent, reachable from main). e5a7e75b is neither, and 3202's tree has a different src/rebar, so f3db stays unflagged: \"Missing tree f3db49d9\".\nEvidence:\n- Local `git pack-objects --thin` of 05c2 with ^a41975c8: 42 objects, 19 external bases; 5 are outside the modelled JGit-marked set, f3db among them. With ^23fdf77f (after fetch): 13 objects, 10 bases, all inside the marked set.\n- Host error_log 10:35:19.682Z: MissingObjectException f3db from FullConnectivityChecker.checkObjects:196 (Gerrit 3.14.1).\n- Host pack-18f26c66 (10:35Z, left over from the rejected push) holds 61 objects = 42 sent + 19 bases appended by JGit, including 05c2, d1a11e74, 8e2201dc, and f3db itself. JGit read f3db to complete the thin pack, then rejected it as unreachable. pack-e51c399b (10:36Z, the accepted retry) holds 23 = 13 + 10.\n- `--no-thin` is a no-op over HTTPS: GIT_TRACE of `git push --dry-run --no-thin gerrit` shows `git send-pack --stateless-rpc ... --thin`. The 10:36Z retry succeeded because of the 10:35:32Z fetch, not the flag. The Group09 failures (2 rejections with --no-thin, 2026-10-23) fit this too.\n- Host (read-only): f3db, 37cf, 490430 all readable. fsck --connectivity-only rc=0 (62 unreachable commits, 71 unreachable trees, 1 unreachable blob). No alternates, no incoming/tmp packs. 363 packs, garbage 0, receive.autogc=false, receive.checkReferencedObjectsAreReachable unset (default true). SSM afad9072-6933-48fa-aef0-c0c792c81fac, 5fb6e6e5-3d99-427a-ba76-463d365e109f.\n- A delta-free pack (`-c pack.window=0 -c pack.depth=0`) of the failing case has 0 external bases.\nConsequence: this is not object-store damage. infra/runbooks/gerrit-object-store-repair.md's snapshot+repair path does not apply when the named object is readable on the host. The fix choice (server knob vs client packing vs fetch-before-push) is escalated to the operator."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793542661760056001,"uuid":"ae88903d-db55-4e41-bf3b-d93506c20124"}